  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-12T15:54:40.637Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have run across multiple scattered instances recently where a youtube video will unexpectedly fail to resolve properly in VRChat. \nThe response for the ytdl resolve sometimes ends up in the format of `n = mJdzf8ySIRvohkGrWt ; player = https://www.youtube.com/s/player/4c3f79c5/player_ias.vflset/en_US/base.js`\nwhich is incorrect and triggers an InvalidUrl video error.\nWhen I tested locally with YTDL (just doing `-g -f best`), I did see it output that line, but immediately after that it logged the valid URL.\nI believe that VRChat is expecting the URL to be on the first info output line or something and doesn't check for additional output lines maybe?\nHere's a URL that is known to fail with these conditions.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3x4D6A12Ql8",
